      <memberdef kind="function" id="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_ini_grouped_resource_1a197fd7cd70ea7f09515c735390d78fe4" prot="public" static="no" const="yes" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="virtual">
        <type>std::vector&lt; <ref refid="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_ini_resource" kindref="compound">IniResource</ref> * &gt;</type>
        <definition>std::vector&lt; IniResource * &gt; AGRemapCore::IniGroupedResource::memberResources</definition>
        <argsstring>() const</argsstring>
        <name>memberResources</name>
        <qualifiedname>AGRemapCore::IniGroupedResource::memberResources</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Every resource this group holds, **borrowed** -- the group keeps ownership, and
the pointers live only as long as it does :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

``virtual``, and that is the whole reason it exists: the `pybind11`_-facing
``PyIniGroupedResource`` stores its members in a `Python`_ ``dict`` keyed by whole
mod objects rather than in #resources, so a caller reading #resources directly
finds every `Python`_-built group empty. Both of the things core does with a
group&apos;s members -- crediting the fix to them, and pushing the
``--compressTextures`` override down into them -- went silently to zero because of
that. Read them through here, never off #resources
</verbatim></para>
<para><simplesect kind="return"><para>Every member resource, in no particular order </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
